-- title:
--   The inclusion I ⊆ J² in Néron's smoothening
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring (a domain, with the discrete valuation ring structure) and $\pi \in R$ an element with $\mathfrak m_R = (\pi)$. Let $C$ and $A$ be commutative rings, each an $R$-algebra, with $A$ a $C$-algebra compatibly with the $R$-structures, and assume the structure map $C \to A$ is surjective. Let $z : \mathrm{Fin}\, n \to C$ be a finite family and put $J = (\pi_C, z_0, \dots, z_{n-1})$, the ideal of $C$ generated by the image $\pi_C$ of $\pi$ together with the range of $z$. Assume: (i) $I := \ker(C \to A) \subseteq J$; (ii) the $n$ elements $1 \otimes d(z_j \bmod I)$ of $(C/J) \otimes_C \Omega^1_{A/R}$ are linearly independent over $C/J$; (iii) the following density condition on $g \in C$: if for every discrete valuation ring $R''$ which is a domain and an $R$-algebra by a local homomorphism, such that $\mathfrak m_R$ generates $\mathfrak m_{R''}$ and the residue field extension $\kappa(R) \to \kappa(R'')$ is formally smooth, and for every $R$-algebra map $c : C \to R''$ with $I \subseteq \ker c$ and $J \subseteq c^{-1}(\mathfrak m_{R''})$, one has $g \in c^{-1}(\mathfrak m_{R''})$, then $g \in J$. The conclusion is $I \subseteq J^2$.
--
--   This is the central inclusion in Néron's smoothening process: with $X = \operatorname{Spec} A$ a closed subscheme of $Z = \operatorname{Spec} C$ and $Y = V(J)$ the centre of a dilatation contained in $X$, it says that the ideal of $X$ lies in the square of the ideal of $Y$, which is what makes the affine dilatation of $Z$ along $Y$ decrease the smoothness defect. It is used in the estimate for the smoothness defect after an affine dilatation at a point of the free locus.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_NeronModelInfra_le_sq_of_linearIndependent_tmul_D_of_forall_indexOne.lean

